    <RoyalTitleDef ParentName="BaseOARKTitle">
        <defName>OA_RK_Title_A</defName>
        <label>Edle</label>
        <description>The Edle is the first level of nobility in Oberonia Aurea's aristocratic system, and there is a distinction between Honorary High Clan and Hereditary Edle. \n\nThough they are nobles, the actual rights of the Edle are not much different from those of the citizens of Oberonia Aurea, but the court will regularly provide additional subsidies for the Edle, and provide additional noble education to the Edles' descendants at an early age in recognition of their past contributions to the Edle. \n\nIn most cases, a citizen of Oberonia Aurea who has spent a lifetime in service to the Court will be given the status of Honorary Edle in her later years, which is not heritable. In addition, if a citizen of Oberonia Aurea has multiple exceptional contributions, there is a chance that he or she will be granted hereditary Edle status.</description>
        <minExpectation>Moderate</minExpectation>
        <changeHeirQuestPoints>1500</changeHeirQuestPoints>
        <recruitmentResistanceOffset>15</recruitmentResistanceOffset>
        <canBeInherited>True</canBeInherited>
        <seniority>150</seniority>
        <favorCost>5</favorCost>
        <commonality>3</commonality>
        <permitPointsAwarded>1</permitPointsAwarded>
        <allowDignifiedMeditationFocus>False</allowDignifiedMeditationFocus>
    </RoyalTitleDef>

    <RoyalTitleDef ParentName="BaseOARKTitle">
        <defName>OA_RK_Title_B</defName>
        <label>Freiherr</label>
        <description>The Freiherr is the second tier of the Oberonia Aurea aristocracy system, and is the highest title that a citizen can achieve without special and great contributions, and there are no rules for honorary titles for the Freiherr and subsequent titles. \n\nCompared to the Edle, the Freiherr could be said to be quite rare, often a city of Oberonia Aurea would only have a few, while cities on remote planets would not even have any. Unlike the Edle, Freiherr have some actual privileges and can demand something from the court as a noble. In addition, Freiherr must also take on some of the responsibilities, commonly assisting the court in maintaining local order, or representing the locality to the court, and so on. \n\nIn the Oberionia Aurea Empire, there is no formulaic way of acquiring the status of Freiherr, unless a hereditary Freiherr has made a rather remarkable contribution to the court, most of the time a new Freiherr title will not be given.</description>
        <minExpectation>High</minExpectation>
        <changeHeirQuestPoints>2000</changeHeirQuestPoints>
        <recruitmentResistanceOffset>30</recruitmentResistanceOffset>
        <requiredMinimumApparelQuality>Normal</requiredMinimumApparelQuality>
        <canBeInherited>True</canBeInherited>
        <seniority>250</seniority>
        <favorCost>15</favorCost>
        <commonality>1</commonality>
        <permitPointsAwarded>1</permitPointsAwarded>
        <allowDignifiedMeditationFocus>False</allowDignifiedMeditationFocus>
        <requiredApparel>
            <li>
                <bodyPartGroupsMatchAny>
                    <li>Torso</li>
                </bodyPartGroupsMatchAny>
                <requiredTags>
                    <li>RoyalTier2</li>
                    <li>Royal</li>
                </requiredTags>
                <allowedTags>
                    <li>Cape</li>
                    <li>PrestigeCombatGear</li>
                    <li>Psychic</li>
                    <li>Mechlord</li>
                </allowedTags>
            </li>
            <li>
